<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila americana detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.117 µm, 0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "k_c, the Jacobian, and the chronoseries formula are named in the module docstring and in the Lean proofs (six theorems, no sorry). Self-test checks the Lean nanometre integers 2117, 1958, and 1900. The Fourier scheme is commented as matching the dispersion operator." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila americana detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.117 µm, 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "onset_kc2 and sigma_plus implement the published critical-wavenumber formula and the larger Jacobian eigenvalue. Kinetics are the cubic activator-inhibitor form. r = 10 is a reconstruction chosen so k_sigma stays near k_c, not a value tabulated by Turing or Wittkopp." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila americana detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.117 µm, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pearson r = 0.989 and RMSE = 0.41 px against lambda(k_sigma). Ablation amplitude ratio is about 0. The detail-scale americana/affinis ratio is below the primordium-scale sibling ratio. The orientation KS is reported but is computed on histogram bins rather than pixel samples, so it is a weak distributional test. n = 1 species card." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
