<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila americana detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.117 µm, 0 Ma) (Drosophila americana)",
        "Drosophila americana detail-scale Turing wavelength (2.117 µm, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila americana morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila americana specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila americana" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim the X–4 fusion or red/brown puparium is a term in the reaction-diffusion equations.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the catalog DOI 10.1016/j.cell.2009.09.044, which Crossref returns as 404.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the repository species card is a micrograph of the ocellus. It is a brown pigment card with a 100 µm scale bar.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Detail-scale wavelengths lambda_i = 2.117e-6 * (L_i / L_americana)^0.35 for affinis, americana, and ananassae.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Physical ruler that sets lambda(k_sigma) = 2.117 µm on the americana anchor.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v with a = 0.1, b = 0.9, r = 10, integrated by a Fourier semi-implicit step.",
        "reported_in_source: Clark et al. 2007 and O'Grady & DeSalle 2018: D. ananassae is in the sequenced Sophophora genomes; D. americana sits in the virilis radiation.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Murray 1981: critical wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v) for a two-species reaction-diffusion system.",
        "reported_in_source: Wittkopp et al. 2009: abdominal pigmentation divergence between D. americana and D. novamexicana is genetic and largely cis-regulatory, at body-color scale.",
        "transfer_boundary: Predecessor and successor are campaign chronoseries neighbors at 0 Ma, not a fossil ancestor-descendant series.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 2.117 µm figure is the assigned detail-scale slot, identified here with the expressed ocellar-pigment wavelength. Wittkopp 2009 does not report that length." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila americana (North American Riparian Willow Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-americana-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_americana_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila americana; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Murray 1981: critical wavenumber k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v) for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Wittkopp et al. 2009: abdominal pigmentation divergence between D. americana and D. novamexicana is genetic and largely cis-regulatory, at body-color scale. | Clark et al. 2007 and O'Grady & DeSalle 2018: D. ananassae is in the sequenced Sophophora genomes; D. americana sits in the virilis radiation.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v with a = 0.1, b = 0.9, r = 10, integrated by a Fourier semi-implicit step. | Detail-scale wavelengths lambda_i = 2.117e-6 * (L_i / L_americana)^0.35 for affinis, americana, and ananassae. | Physical ruler that sets lambda(k_sigma) = 2.117 µm on the americana anchor.; transfer_boundary: The 2.117 µm figure is the assigned detail-scale slot, identified here with the expressed ocellar-pigment wavelength. Wittkopp 2009 does not report that length. | Predecessor and successor are campaign chronoseries neighbors at 0 Ma, not a fossil ancestor-descendant series.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the repository species card is a micrograph of the ocellus. It is a brown pigment card with a 100 µm scale bar. | Does not claim the X–4 fusion or red/brown puparium is a term in the reaction-diffusion equations. | Does not claim the catalog DOI 10.1016/j.cell.2009.09.044, which Crossref returns as 404.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1176980>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1534/genetics.117.300583> ;
